# Restless Vinestalk: "up to one other target creature has base power and toughness 3/3 until end of turn" sets the base
# (CR 613.4b), so a +1/+1 counter still applies on top (613.4c): Bot1's own Walking Ballista (X = 1, a 1/1 with a counter) is
# 4/4 after the attack trigger, and the Vinestalk itself is not a legal target of its own "other" (refused beside the
# Ballista). "Until end of turn" ends all of it: by Bot2's turn 4 the Ballista is a 1/1 again and the land is only a land.

[Bot1 Deck]
Restless Vinestalk
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Walking Ballista
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Restless Vinestalk.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Walking Ballista.Cast(X: 1)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Restless Vinestalk.Activate(Ability: becomes a 5/5)
Bot1.Attack(Restless Vinestalk > Bot2)
! Bot1.Target(Restless Vinestalk)
Bot1.Target(Walking Ballista)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Walking Ballista.Power = 4
? Bot1.Battlefield.Walking Ballista.Toughness = 4
[T4 Bot2.Upkeep]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Walking Ballista.Power = 1
? Bot1.Battlefield.Restless Vinestalk.Types = Land

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 15
Bot1.Battlefield.Walking Ballista.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
